  "user_request_original": "Design a 20-layer planar dielectric filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Materials: alternating Ta2O5 (high index) and SiO2 (low index), starting with Ta2O5 at air interface and ending with SiO2 at substrate. Wavelength bands: passband at 1550 nm (target high transmittance), stopbands at 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm (target low transmittance). Initialize layers 1-8 thicknesses to Round 4 optimized values: [158.50, 268.40, 158.30, 268.20, 158.10, 268.00, 157.90, 267.90] nm and freeze these during optimization. Initialize layers 9-20 to Round 4 values: [147.80, 257.70, 147.60, 257.50, 148.00, 258.00, 148.00, 258.00, 148.00, 258.00, 148.00, 270.81] nm with optimization bounds ±20 nm. Apply gradient-based thickness optimization with layer-index-dependent learning rates: even-indexed layers (SiO2) use 0.5x learning rate relative to odd-indexed layers (Ta2O5). Optimize for maximum transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in both stopbands. Total layer count fixed at 20. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 20-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica for maximum transmittance at 1550 nm while minimizing transmittance in 1400–1500 nm and 1600–1700 nm, freezing the first eight layer thicknesses and allowing ±20 nm variation on the remaining twelve.",
